1
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:23,500
This summer a star falls. The chase begins.

2
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Stardust is a adventure, fantasy, romance film directed by Matthew Vaughn.

3
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:58,500
In a countryside town bordering on a magical land, a young man makes a promise to his
beloved that he'll retrieve a fallen star by venturing into the magical realm.

4
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:16,000
His journey takes him into a world beyond his wildest
dreams and reveals his true identity.

5
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:33,500
Tristan Thorn, played by Charlie Cox.

6
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Yvaine, played by Claire Danes.

7
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:08,500
Lamia, played by Michelle Pfeiffer.

8
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:26,000
Septimus, played by Mark Strong.

9
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:43,500
Primus, played by Jason Flemyng.

10
00:52:55,000 --> 00:53:01,000
Captain Shakespeare, played by Robert De Niro.

11
00:58:12,500 --> 00:58:18,500
Stardust is a 2007 romantic fantasy adventure film directed by
Matthew Vaughn and co-written by Vaughn and Jane Goldman.

12
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
Based on Neil Gaiman's 1999 novel, it features an ensemble cast led by Claire Danes, Charlie Cox, Sienna Miller, Ricky Gervais,
Jason Flemyng, Rupert Everett, Peter O'Toole, Michelle Pfeiffer and Robert De Niro, with narration by Ian McKellen.

13
01:08:47,500 --> 01:08:53,500
The film follows Tristan, a young man from the
fictional town of Wall in England.

14
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:11,000
Wall is a town on the border of the magical fantasy kingdom of Stormhold.

15
01:19:22,500 --> 01:19:28,500
Tristan enters the magical world to collect a fallen star to give to his
beloved Victoria, in return for her hand in marriage.

16
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
To his surprise, he collects the star, a woman named Yvaine.

17
01:29:57,500 --> 01:30:03,500
Witches and the Princes of Stormhold are also hunting for Yvaine.

18
01:35:15,000 --> 01:35:21,000
Meanwhile, Tristan tries to get her back to Wall with him before
Victoria's birthday, the deadline for her offer.

19
01:40:32,500 --> 01:40:38,500
The film was released to positive reviews and grossed
$137 million on a $70–88.5 million budget.

20
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:56,000
In 2008 it won the Hugo Award for Best Dramatic Presentation, Long Form.

21
01:51:07,500 --> 01:51:13,500
It was released on DVD, Blu-ray and HD DVD on 18 December 2007.

22
01:56:25,000 --> 01:56:31,000
The film explores themes of witch, new love, based on
novel or book, kingdom, transformation.

23
02:01:42,500 --> 02:01:48,500
The tone is emotional.
